        <h4 data-i18n="p3_title" class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">
          CS Interactive Workshop
        </h4>

        <p data-i18n="p3_desc" class="text-slate-300 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed mb-5">
          Interactive web workshop for Computer Science students at the University of Costa Rica, covering algorithms and data structures, parallel and concurrent programming, networking, technical interview patterns, SQL, and Git through live simulations backed by real C and C++ engines. Each station guides students through experimenting with a simulation, understanding the theory, and studying the native implementation: POSIX semaphores, a 2D heat diffusion solver in serial, pthreads, and OpenMP versions with bit-for-bit identical results, a multi-threaded TCP server, and a Git station whose objects are hashed exactly like real Git. It grew out of my own coursework projects (a sorting visualizer, a concurrency lab, and a distributed ASCII art server), which now run as its engines. Deployed on Firebase Hosting through a CI pipeline that runs 1,538 automated tests.
        </p>

